rom Tanzania: the first 2 Italian cases from a small outbreak among European travellers.</article-title><source>Clin Infect Dis</source><volume>34</volume><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>22</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000238-Moore1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Escombe</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Agranoff</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Bailey</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Squire</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Chiodini</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>African trypanosomiasis in travellers returning to the United Kingdom.</article-title><source>Emerg Infect Dis</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>74</fpage><lpage>76</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11749752</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000238-Poltera2"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Poltera</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1985</year><article-title>Pathology of human African trypanosomiasis with reference to experimental African trypanosomiasis and infections of the central nervous system.</article-title><source>Br Med Bull</source><volume>41</volume><fpage>169</fpage><lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3896375</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000238-Fevre1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fevre</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name><name><surname>Coleman</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><name><surname>Welburn</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Maudlin</surname><given-names>I</given-name